metadata:
  project: E36 Restomod -- Radium 20-1170 Fuel Pump Hanger Wiring (PHASE 1)
  phase: "Phase 1 (M52 + M50 pre-terminated harness era — no PMU16 in car yet)"
  description: >-
    PHASE 1 fuel pump wiring: Radium 20-1170 hanger + Walbro F90000267 (E85-safe,
    465 LPH) driven by a DISCRETE aftermarket high-current relay in the engine bay.
    Relay coil is triggered by the MaxxECU M50 pre-terminated harness's fuel pump
    signal wire. This is the industry-standard approach for high-current aftermarket
    fuel pumps — see vendor citation below.

    Why a discrete relay in Phase 1: PMU16 is NOT installed until Phase 3
    (07K swap moment). Under Phase 1, MaxxECU RACE H2O is engine-bay-mounted but
    it drives its GPO outputs at low current (~150 mA typical) — it cannot directly
    carry the pump's ~14-17 A running current. And the OEM K6301 Fuel Pump Relay
    that this circuit REPLACES is designed for the ~5-10 A OEM in-tank pump, at
    the upper edge of its rating with a Walbro F90000267. Motorsport convention
    is a dedicated aftermarket relay + fuse + heavier gauge wire (per JDT Racing
    Rewire Kit vendor guidance below).

    Pump current draw citation:
      walbrofuelpumps.com/450lph-walbro-e85-racing-fuel-pump-f90000267.html
      "465 lph @ 40 psi and 13.5V (14.1 amps) in gasoline"
      (E85 slightly higher due to fuel density — plan for ~15-17 A running current)

    Convention citation (aftermarket rewire kit):
      jdtracing.com/products/walbro-ti-f90000267-450lph-fuel-pump-w-install-kit-rewire-kit-e85-compatible
      "One of the most common mistakes people make when trying to run a high volume
       fuel pump is trying to use the factory wiring which on most vehicles is
       extremely inadequate. When installing a much larger than factory fuel pump
       you need to upgrade the wiring, fuse and relay setup."
      The JDT Racing Rewire Kit includes: new relay, 30A inline fuse, 10 AWG wire,
      pass-through grommet, ring terminals. Same architecture used here.

    Phase 3 transition: at 07K swap moment, this discrete relay is REMOVED and
    replaced by PMU16 O4 direct-drive. See harnesses/fuel-pump-hanger-phase3.wv.
    The 12 AWG cabin/tunnel wire from firewall grommet → tunnel → hanger pump(+)
    stud stays in place — only the engine-bay end changes (relay contact →
    PMU16 O4). Minimal Phase 3 rewiring.

    OEM E36 fuel pump routing (that this wire mirrors): K6301 Fuel Pump Relay pin 87
    (engine-bay Front Power Distribution Box) → X20 pin 13 → cabin body harness →
    trunk/tank → in-tank pump. Source: E36 ETM section 0670.2 via
    carmanualsonline.info/bmw-318is-1999-e36-electrical-troubleshooting-manual.
    Under our Phase 1 arch, the discrete added relay REPLACES the K6301 relay
    function; X20 pin 13 (previously the OEM fuel pump feed) is cavity-plugged.

    Cross-reference fuel-pump-hanger-reference.md for pump/hanger specs
    and MTune config (fuel pump signal function assignment).
    Install PDF: radiumauto.com/pages/instructions (20-1170).

# ── TODO list ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   [ ] Verify F90000267 fits chosen Radium hanger slot -- 39mm/50mm DCSS body confirmed
#   [ ] Source discrete high-current relay -- Bosch/Hella 0332-002-156 or equiv (40/70A rating)
#   [ ] Source 30A inline blade fuse holder + fuse
#   [ ] Confirm MaxxECU M50 harness fuel pump signal wire identification
#       Reference: docs/vendor/maxxecu/MaxxECU_M50_Terminated_Harness.md
#       Typical: GPO on the 16-pin aux breakout or a dedicated harness stub
#   [ ] Assign MaxxECU MTune fuel pump output function to the GPO driving the coil
#       MTune: Outputs -> Output config -> Function: Fuel Pump (or PWM fuel pump if desired)
#   [ ] Confirm 12 AWG run length (engine bay relay → tunnel → tank hanger, est. 3.5-4m)
#       Add 20% slack per BOM conventions; pre-terminate before routing through tunnel
#   [ ] Thread 20-1000-1010 swivel fitting (10AN ORB) into pump-out port HAND-TIGHT
#       then attach -10AN braided line before final torque -- allows rotation to route
#   [ ] Return port: use included 8.5mm barb adapter (OEM return line)
#       OR add 20-1000-0606 (6AN ORB swivel) if converting to full AN return
#   [ ] Dedicate chassis GND stud for pump(-) -- do not share with ECU sensor grounds

# ── Connectors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

connectors:

  MAXXECU_GPO_FP:
    type: "MaxxECU M50 pre-terminated harness — 12-pin extra connector pin 3 (GPO 2)"
    subtype: "Low-side GPO 2 output (~150 mA), drives relay coil pin 85"
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["GPO 2 signal (low-side switch to GND)"]
    notes: >
      MaxxECU GPO 2 low-side output — sinks to GND when fuel pump is commanded on.
      Does NOT supply +12V. MTune Function: "Fuel pump relay" (binary on/off in Phase 1).
      Exposed on the M50 pre-terminated harness's 12-pin EXTRA connector at pin 3
      (ECU_12PIN pin 3). This is the canonical Phase 1 fuel pump path per the
      walkthrough at e36-docs/walkthroughs/08-fuel-system.md step 9 and
      e36-docs/walkthroughs/11-ecu-chassis-wiring.md relay block spec.
      Source: docs/vendor/maxxecu/MaxxECU_M50_Terminated_Harness.md §12-pin extra.
      Phase 3: this GPO 2 assignment moves to a MaxxECU CAN broadcast that PMU16
      subscribes to; PMU16 O4 direct-drives the pump. See fuel-pump-hanger-phase3.wv.

  FP_RELAY:
    type: "Discrete high-current relay (40A / 70A dual-rating ISO mini)"
    subtype: "Bosch 0 332 002 156 or Hella equivalent — 12V coil, dual contact"
    pincount: 5
    pinlabels:
      - "85 Coil - (MaxxECU GPO low-side)"
      - "86 Coil + (+12V OEM IGN)"
      - "87 Contact NO out → cabin/tunnel wire → hanger"
      - "87a Contact NC (unused, cap or clip off)"
      - "30 Battery+ (fused via 30A inline)"
    notes: >
      40A/70A dual-rating relay gives ~2x headroom over the Walbro F90000267 running
      current (~14-17A). Coil draws ~150 mA — well within MaxxECU GPO output spec.
      Mount in engine bay alongside the existing OEM Front Power Distribution Box
      or on a fabricated bracket near the MaxxECU RACE H2O.

      Flyback diode: 1N4007 across relay coil.
        Cathode (banded end) → pin 86 / +12V.
        Anode → pin 85 / GPO.
      Prevents GPO output damage from coil back-EMF at relay de-energization.

      Phase 3 transition: this relay is REMOVED at 07K swap. PMU16 O4 replaces it —
      the O4 output wire lands on the same cabin/tunnel wire that this relay's
      contact pin 87 currently feeds. See fuel-pump-hanger-phase3.wv.

  FP_FUSE:
    type: "30A blade fuse holder (inline, engine-bay-mounted)"
    subtype: "MTA/Littelfuse 30A ATO/ATC blade with weatherproof inline holder"
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["+12V fused to relay pin 30"]
    notes: >
      30A rating matches JDT Racing Rewire Kit vendor spec for this exact pump.
      Mount within 12" of battery positive to protect the entire relay+wire path.
      Weatherproof inline holder recommended for engine-bay location.

  RADIUM_HANGER:
    type: "Radium Engineering 20-1170 — stainless stud electrical terminals"
    subtype: "Top-plate external studs — anti-rotation, hermetically sealed"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels:
      - "Pump(+) — switched +12V from relay contact 87"
      - "Pump(-) — chassis GND"
    notes: >
      Radium 20-1170 uses custom stainless steel studs through the top plate (not a
      multi-pin connector). External connection via ring terminals + anodized acorn nuts.
      Anti-rotation feature prevents stud from spinning during install.
      Hermetically sealed and impervious to E85, gasoline, methanol.
      Ring terminals: 12 AWG crimp ring, M4 or M5 stud diameter (confirm at install).
      In-tank wiring insulated with ETFE — chemically resistant to all fuel types.
      Single pump install (F90000267): run 12 AWG from relay pin 87 to pump(+) stud
      (Phase 1) or from PMU16 O4 to pump(+) stud (Phase 3 — same wire, upstream end
      changes).
      Hanger: https://www.radiumauto.com/products/bmw-e36-fuel-pump-hanger
      Pump: https://www.walbrofuelpumps.com/product/f90000267/

  BATT_POS:
    type: "Battery positive stud (engine bay side of cutoff switch)"
    subtype: "Post-cutoff +12V constant supply"
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["+12V BATT (post-cutoff, fused via FP_FUSE 30A)"]

  IGN_12V_BODY:
    type: "OEM ignition relay — body harness switched +12V"
    subtype: "Relay coil supply (pin 86)"
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["+12V IGN (body harness)"]
    notes: >
      Same OEM IGN relay rail used by fan relay and OEM fuel pump relay coils.
      Coil draws ~150 mA at 12V — negligible load.

  CHASSIS_GND:
    type: "Chassis ground stud (body metal, near fuel tank)"
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["GND"]
    notes: >-
      Dedicated ground for pump(-) terminal on Radium hanger.
      Do not share with ECU sensor grounds or other high-current grounds.
      12 AWG minimum. Ring terminal, solid bolt to body metal.

# ── Cables ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

cables:

  W_GPO_COIL:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [GN]
    wirelabels: ["MaxxECU GPO → relay pin 85 (coil low-side)"]
    length: 0.5 m
    notes: >
      Engine-bay-only run from MaxxECU M50 harness fuel pump signal exit to relay
      pin 85. 18 AWG sufficient — carries ~150 mA coil current only.

  W_COIL_PWR:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [RD]
    wirelabels: ["+12V IGN → relay pin 86 (coil +)"]
    length: 0.3 m
    notes: "OEM IGN relay +12V to relay pin 86. 18 AWG."

  W_FUSE_TO_RELAY:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [RD]
    wirelabels: ["+12V battery via 30A fuse → relay pin 30"]
    length: 0.5 m
    notes: >
      From battery+ stud through 30A inline fuse to relay pin 30 (contact input).
      10 AWG (matches JDT Racing Rewire Kit spec — provides low voltage drop at
      peak current).

  W_PUMP_PWR:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [RD]
    wirelabels: ["Relay pin 87 → cabin grommet → tunnel → tank hanger pump(+)"]
    length: 4.0 m
    notes: >
      Relay contact output (pin 87) → dedicated firewall grommet → cabin body
      harness route (mirrors OEM E36 fuel pump path) → back to trunk/tank →
      Radium hanger pump(+) stud.
      12 AWG minimum. Route through transmission tunnel. Keep clear of exhaust
      where tunnel-side routing is close to heat. Loom in expandable braid for
      this full run. Estimated run: 3.5-4m -- measure on car, add 20% slack
      before cutting.
      Phase 3: this SAME WIRE stays in place. Only the relay-end lands on
      PMU16 O4 instead of relay pin 87. Minimal Phase 3 rework.

  W_PUMP_GND:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [BK]
    wirelabels: ["Radium hanger pump(-) → chassis GND"]
    length: 0.5 m
    notes: >
      Radium hanger pump(-) stud to chassis ground stud. 12 AWG.
      Dedicated ground — do not share with ECU sensor ground bus.
      Ring terminal at both ends.

# ── Connections ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

connections:

  # ── Relay coil circuit ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # MaxxECU GPO sinks pin 85 to GND when fuel pump active. Pin 86 is +12V IGN.
  - - MAXXECU_GPO_FP: [1]
    - W_GPO_COIL: [1]
    - FP_RELAY: [1]           # pin 85 — low-side

  - - IGN_12V_BODY: [1]
    - W_COIL_PWR: [1]
    - FP_RELAY: [2]           # pin 86 — coil +

  # ── Relay contact circuit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Battery+ → 30A fuse → relay pin 30 → relay pin 87 → cabin/tunnel wire → pump.
  - - BATT_POS: [1]
    - W_FUSE_TO_RELAY: [1]
    - FP_RELAY: [5]           # pin 30 — contact in (via fuse)

  - - FP_RELAY: [3]           # pin 87 — contact out
    - W_PUMP_PWR: [1]
    - RADIUM_HANGER: [1]      # pump(+) stud

  # ── Pump GND circuit ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - - RADIUM_HANGER: [2]      # pump(-) stud
    - W_PUMP_GND: [1]
    - CHASSIS_GND: [1]
